{"review":"approved","flags":[{"page":58,"note":"The quantities labelled 'Std.Dev' (6.23, 0.03) are variances (the formula has no square root); the SDs are 2.50 and 0.16. The next slide lists cluster-1 SDs as (6.32, 0.03), which looks like a transposition of 6.23."},{"page":56,"note":"The membership lines say 'P(Z Doc1-Cluster1) = 0.006 / 0.994' but they belong to Doc2 (the calculation shown above them)."},{"page":57,"note":"'At one iteration it will approach a very large value' describes the GMM singularity: with a component collapsing onto one document the likelihood grows without bound. Real implementations floor the variance; growth of the log-likelihood should not be read as convergence here."},{"page":31,"note":"Mixture models do not create a 'convex' search space: the GMM log-likelihood is non-concave with many local optima, which is why EM needs several restarts."}],"recall":{"defs":[["Clustering","Grouping unlabelled objects by similarity."],["K-means","Hard clustering minimising within-cluster squared distances."],["K-medoids","K-means variant with actual objects as centres."],["GMM","Weighted sum of Gaussian components."],["Responsibility","Posterior probability that a component generated a point."],["EM","Alternating expectation and maximisation for latent-variable MLE."]],"formulas":["J=\\sum_{n}\\sum_{k}r_{nk}\\|x_n-\\mu_k\\|^2","\\mu_k=\\frac{\\sum_nr_{nk}x_n}{\\sum_nr_{nk}}","p(x)=\\sum_k\\pi_k\\mathcal N(x|\\mu_k,\\Sigma_k)","\\gamma(z_{nk})=\\frac{\\pi_k\\mathcal N(x_n|\\mu_k,\\Sigma_k)}{\\sum_j\\pi_j\\mathcal N(x_n|\\mu_j,\\Sigma_j)}","\\mu_k=\\frac1{N_k}\\sum_n\\gamma(z_{nk})x_n,\\ \\pi_k=\\frac{N_k}N"],"takeaways":["K-means: assign to nearest centre, move centres to means, repeat.","Use restarts and the elbow; scale features.","K-means fails on unequal sizes/densities, odd shapes, outliers; K-medoids for outliers.","GMMs give soft memberships and elliptical clusters.","EM: responsibilities → weighted MLE of π, μ, Σ; watch for collapsing components."],"confused":[["E-step in K-means vs GMM","Nearest centre vs responsibilities."],["SD vs variance in the EM example","The M-step yields variances."],["Hard vs soft","0/1 vs probabilities."],["SSE vs log-likelihood","K-means vs GMM objective."]],"minute":"Unsupervised learning groups unlabelled data. K-means minimises the within-cluster sum of squared distances by alternating an E-step (assign each point to its nearest centre) and an M-step (move each centre to its cluster mean); it converges to a local minimum, so use restarts and choose K with the elbow of SSE. It struggles with clusters of different sizes, densities, non-globular shapes and outliers; K-medoids is more robust to outliers, and distance ratios flag outliers. Gaussian mixture models give soft memberships: p(x) = Σ π_k N(μ_k, Σ_k). EM computes responsibilities, then re-estimates weights, means and covariances, until the log-likelihood stabilises."},"flashcards":[["K-means objective","$J=\\sum_n\\sum_kr_{nk}\\|x_n-\\mu_k\\|^2$",6],["E-step (K-means)","Assign to nearest centre",9],["M-step (K-means)","$\\mu_k=\\frac{\\sum r_{nk}x_n}{\\sum r_{nk}}$",10],["SSE","Sum of squared distances to cluster centres",16],["K-means limits","Sizes, densities, shapes, outliers",21],["K-medoids","Most central actual object as centre",25],["Elbow method","SSE vs K; pick the bend",26],["Outlier score","$\\text{dist}(x,\\mu_k)/L_{\\mu_k}$",27],["1-of-K coding","Each row of r has one 1",30],["Gaussian pdf","$\\frac1{\\sigma\\sqrt{2\\pi}}e^{-\\frac12(\\frac{x-\\mu}\\sigma)^2}$",33],["GMM density","$\\sum_k\\pi_k\\mathcal N(x|\\mu_k,\\Sigma_k)$",48],["Responsibility","$\\gamma_{nk}=\\frac{\\pi_k\\mathcal N_k}{\\sum_j\\pi_j\\mathcal N_j}$",50],["N_k","$\\sum_n\\gamma(z_{nk})$",52],["π update","$N_k/N$",52],["covariance_type","full, tied, diag, spherical",60]],"coverage":{"topics":[{"simple":["what"],"deep":["u-intro"],"viz":[],"status":"complete"},{"simple":["h1"],"deep":["u-kmeans"],"viz":["kmeansStepper"],"status":"comple